{
  "about": "The versionCode a release tag was built with. 'codes': launcher tags, as the launcher (SelfUpdatePlanTest, launcherTagVersionCode) and the server (install_now::launcher_tag_version_code) read them; code null = not a launcher release tag (a music tag included). 'music_codes': music tags with the version the server's About This Phone shows for that code (handlers::device_pages::version_of_code). scripts/release-version.sh --selftest reads both lists' rows without '@': a tag it builds gets the row's code, a row from the first tag under today's rule on is built, an older one refused. Today's rule, from launcher-v0.36.0-rc.4 and music-v0.5.0-rc.4 on: X*10_000_000 + Y*10_000 + Z*10 + N, N = the RC number 1..8, 9 for the release; X <= 199, Y and Z <= 999. Tags below it were built under the old rule, X*1_000_000 + Y*1_000 + Z, an RC one less, and read so (every real tag before the cutover is a row). The part from '@' on (the server's release id) is ignored. Two byte-identical copies: server/testdata/launcher_tag_codes.json and launcher/app/src/test/resources/launcher_tag_codes.json; each suite fails if the other copy is missing or differs. Change both together.",
